{"format_version":1,"partition":893,"records":{"-bar":{"entries":[["-bar",null,"/baːɐ̯/","From Middle High German -bære, from Old High German -bāri, from Proto-Germanic *bēriz.\nThe modern vowel -a- is after the adverb form (Middle High German -bāre, Old High German -bāro), which came to be used in predicative and then also in attributive position. This development was especially Low and Central German (compare Middle Low German -bār(e) alongside -bēr(e)). Also cognate with Dutch -baar, West Frisian -ber, Alemannic German -bar, Old English -bǣre. Old Norse -bærr (Old Swedish -bǣr). This suffix is said to be West Germanic, so the Old Norse form is probably an early Middle Low German borrowing."]],"senses":[[52687,"-bar","suffix","-able, -ible",0]]},"abbeissend":{"entries":[["abbeissend",null,null,null]],"senses":[[368860,"abbeissend","verb","present participle of abbeissen",0]],"inflections":[["abbeissend","abbeissen","participle,present"]]},"abderitischem":{"entries":[["abderitischem",null,null,null]],"senses":[[442687,"abderitischem","adj","strong dative masculine/neuter singular of abderitisch",0]],"inflections":[["abderitischem","abderitisch","dative,masculine,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"affentittengeiler":{"entries":[["affentittengeiler",null,null,null]],"senses":[[446209,"affentittengeiler","adj","comparative degree of affentittengeil",0],[446210,"affentittengeiler","adj","inflection of affentittengeil:",1],[446211,"affentittengeiler","adj","strong/mixed nominative masculine singular",2],[446212,"affentittengeiler","adj","strong genitive/dative feminine singular",3],[446213,"affentittengeiler","adj","strong genitive plural",4]],"inflections":[["affentittengeiler","affentittengeil","masculine,nominative,singular,strong"]]},"anstachelte":{"entries":[["anstachelte",null,null,null]],"senses":[[132832,"anstachelte","verb","inflection of anstacheln:",0],[132833,"anstachelte","verb","first/third-person singular dependent preterite",1],[132834,"anstachelte","v